Return `effects().ignore()` for event types you don't handle. Only let real processing errors propagate, because an exception triggers redelivery.

```java
public Effect onEvent(CounterEvent event) {
  return switch (event) {
    case CounterEvent.ValueIncreased v -> { /* handle */ yield effects().done(); }
    default -> effects().ignore();   // not interested, so skip
  };
}
```

If a `switch` over a sealed type has no `default`, add one, or list the unwanted cases explicitly and map them to `ignore()`. Also make the handled path idempotent, since delivery is at-least-once.

